      origins: "Trappola originated in Venice (Cardano, 1564) and spread to Central Europe, where it developed many variations. Stovkahra (Brčko) is a surviving form played in the Czech village of Šumice in Romania's Banát region. Researched by Tomáš Svoboda in 1997 and published in The Playing-Card; it retains Trappola point values and bonuses using a German 32-card pack after original Trappola cards ceased production in 1944.",
