          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first team to score 100 or more points. Points are scored for declared combinations (three or four of a rank), for cards taken in tricks (Ace 6, King 5, Ober 4, Unter 3; tens and below 0), and as bonuses for winning the last trick (6), a middle trick with a seven (10), the last trick with a seven (26), or the first trick with a seven (52).',
          gameplay: 'Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite). Deal 8 cards each (3-2-3); bottom card of the pack is shown and its suit is trumps. Before the first trick, players may declare combinations (three or four aces, tens, sevens, kings, or knaves) for points; only declared combinations count. Player to dealer\'s left leads. Must follow suit; if unable, must play a trump. Must beat the highest card in the trick if possible. Trick is won by the highest trump, or highest of led suit if no trump. Winner of each trick leads to the next. A player may call "dost" (enough) when their team believes they have reached 100 points to stop play and count; if correct they win the game (1 or 2 brčka depending on opponents\' score); if wrong the opponents win 2 brčka. First team to 10 brček wins the series.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit; if void in led suit must play a trump.',
            'Must beat the current highest card in the trick if able.',
            'Only declared combinations (stated before first trick) are scored.',
            'First team to 100 points wins the deal; call "dost" to stop play and count.',
            'First team to 10 brček (matchsticks) wins the series.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Count trumps. Declare marriages early for points. Lead aces to draw out tens. Don't waste trumps on small tricks.",
          intermediate: 'Signaling: Discards can indicate strength.',
          advanced: 'The Endplay: Knowing exactly how many points represent the remaining cards allows for perfect squeeze plays. If you need 4 points to win and you have a King...',
          tips: [
            'Tens are high (A > 10 > K).',
            'Marriages are huge swings.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
